<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badlay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1445</span> · Also known as Sultan Badlay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Badlay was a sultan of Adal who led a war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> in the fifteenth century. He was killed in 1445 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gomit">Battle of Gomit</a>, where his forces were defeated by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zara-yaqob">Zara Yaqob</a>. His death was a severe setback for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>.</p></div>
